        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "chore: eliminate unchecked TypeScript test casts",
        "body": "Closes #105764\n\n## What Problem This Solves\n\nTypeScript tests and harnesses accumulated unchecked `as any` casts, allowing fixture drift and invalid mock shapes to bypass the compiler. The existing suppression count was also a point-in-time observation rather than a repository gate.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nReplace all tracked test/harness `as any` and `<any>` assertions with owner types, inferred parameter/return types, typed fixture helpers, or narrow `unknown` boundaries. Add an AST-based tracked-file inventory so unchecked casts stay at zero, while keeping only five `@ts-expect-error` directives that directly exercise Kysely's negative literal contracts.\n\n## User Impact\n\nNo runtime behavior change. Maintainers get stricter compile-time validation for test fixtures and an automated regression gate for suppression debt.\n\n## Evidence\n\n- Before: 508 AST-detected unchecked any assertions and 8 `@ts-expect-error` directives in the current tracked source/test inventory.\n- After: 0 `as any`, 0 `<any>`, and 5 explicit Kysely negative-contract directives across 18,497 tracked TypeScript files.\n- Blacksmith Testbox `tbx_01kxcbxs7fg73sscf58g175s23`: all 50 touched test files passed across 23 Vitest shards.\n- `pnpm check:test-types` passed.\n- Full `pnpm check:changed` exercised formatting, dependency, SDK surface, typecheck, and lint lanes. Its sole finding was an unnecessary test-helper type parameter; after fixing it, targeted extension lint and `pnpm tsgo:extensions:test` passed.\n- Final focused proof: runtime-agent and Telegram helper tests passed (111 tests), core/extension test typechecks passed, and the suppression inventory remained 0/0/5.\n- Fresh autoreview after the final fix: no accepted/actionable findings.\n",
        "branch": "codex/reduce-test-type-suppressions",
